## Overview

Implemented secure remote server access by setting up SSH key-based authentication with added passphrase protection to improve security during server configuration and management.

## Components

Access Method      | SSH Key Authentication
Security Layer     | Passphrase-Protected Key
Protocol           | OpenSSH
Environment        | Remote Server Setup
User Access        | Terminal-Based Remote Login

## Process

Generated and configured SSH key pairs for secure authentication to a remote server. Added a passphrase to the private key to enhance security in case of key exposure. Installed the public key on the server and disabled or avoided password-based login during setup. Used SSH for secure remote administration while configuring and managing server services. Verified successful authentication and stable remote access after configuration.

